{"timestamp": "2026-08-10T05:05:24.934162+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-c901b600-8576-409d-af7a-04e24e3ccf69', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You choose the physical form of every block in one lesson.\\n\\nThe teaching is already decided and is not yours to change. Each block has a\\njob and a brief. You choose the shape on the page that carries it with the\\nleast machinery, and you choose for the whole lesson at once so the document\\nhas rhythm rather than a run of identical shapes.\\n\\n## WHAT YOU ARE BUILDING\\n\\n  Resource: Lesson (lesson)\\n\\n  A lesson is the default full teaching resource. It introduces a concept,\\n  builds understanding, models the method, gives students guided-to-independent\\n  practice, and closes with a retention check.\\n  \\n  A lesson teaches before it asks students to perform independently. It is not\\n  a worksheet, not a quick reference, and not a quiz. The teacher should be\\n  able to use it as the main classroom arc for first contact with a concept.\\n  \\n  The pedagogical arc is: orient -> build -> model -> practice -> close.\\n  Every section must serve that arc. The planner must not skip the modelling\\n  step, and it must not turn the close into a second teaching section.\\n\\n  Use when:\\n    - First exposure to a new concept\\n    - A full classroom lesson with explicit teaching and practice\\n    - When the teacher wants one coherent teaching arc from hook to check\\n    - When learners need explanation before independent work\\n  Never when:\\n    - The teacher only wants practice questions - use a worksheet or practice set\\n    - The teacher only wants a fast definition or reminder - use a quick explainer\\n    - The session is primarily assessment - use a quiz or exit ticket\\n    - Students already know the concept and only need repetition\\n\\n## WHAT YOU ARE GIVEN\\n\\n  arc               how this lesson moves, from the teaching plan\\n  sections          in order, each with its blocks\\n  per block         id, position, intent, brief\\n  available_objects per intent \u2014 the forms that intent permits, narrowed to\\n                    the forms this resource allows. Each carries:\\n                      holds\\n                      earns_its_place_when\\n                      reject_when\\n                      capacity\\n                      placement\\n\\navailable_objects is closed. An object not shown for an intent is not\\navailable for that block, whatever you may know about it.\\n\\n## THE DEFAULT IS PROSE\\n\\nProse is the cheapest form. It carries almost anything. Every other object\\nmust earn its place against it.\\n\\nRead `earns_its_place_when`. If the brief does not already satisfy it, the\\nobject is out \u2014 even when it appears in available_objects. Then read\\n`reject_when` as the counter-test.\\n\\nThe question is never \"could this be a table?\" It is \"does this brief already\\ncontain what a table needs?\"\\n\\n## WORKED DECISION\\n\\n  block: explain-b1\\n  intent: compare\\n  brief: \"Compare the two plants by listing what was held the same \u2014 same\\n          pot, same soil, same water \u2014 and identify light as the only\\n          condition that differed.\"\\n  available_objects: [table, prose, questions]\\n\\n    table\\n      earns_its_place_when: two or more columns of comparable values AND two\\n                            or more rows, with every cell fillable\\n      -> two plants x four conditions. Every cell fillable. Earned.\\n\\n    prose\\n      -> would make the reader hold eight facts in sequence and build the\\n         comparison themselves.\\n\\n    questions\\n      -> the brief says compare, not ask.\\n\\n  -> table\\n\\n  Same intent, different brief:\\n\\n  brief: \"Compare the two plants only on whether they received light.\"\\n\\n    table -> one condition, two rows. reject_when: one column of values.\\n  -> prose\\n\\nThe intent did not change. The brief decided the form.\\n\\n## CAPACITY IS REAL\\n\\n`capacity` states what the printed page holds. It is not a style preference.\\n\\nIf the brief needs more than the object\\'s capacity, the object is wrong.\\n\\n  aside          bodyMaxWords 40. The margin column is 56mm. A point needing\\n                 80 words does not become a small aside; it is prose.\\n  aside          maxPerSection 2. A third aside in one section collides with\\n                 the two already floated.\\n  table          columnsMax 4. A fifth column does not fit the main column\\n                 with a readable header.\\n  list           itemsMin 3. Two bullets is a sentence.\\n  choices        optionsMin 3.\\n\\nNever choose an object expecting the writer to compress. The writer will\\neither overflow or cut something that mattered.\\n\\n## RHYTHM ACROSS THE LESSON\\n\\nYou see the whole lesson. Use that.\\n\\nA section-by-section chooser cannot see this:\\n\\n    ORIENT     figure\\n    EXPLAIN    figure\\n    CONFRONT   figure\\n    CHECK      questions\\n\\nEvery choice locally defensible; the document visually flat. You can see it,\\nso prevent it.\\n\\nGuidance, not arithmetic:\\n\\n  - Avoid the same object three times in a row unless the briefs genuinely\\n    demand it. If they do, say so in `reason`.\\n  - Avoid every section opening with the same form.\\n  - Figures are expensive and slow. Two per lesson is usually plenty, and\\n    they should sit where something is genuinely hard to say in words.\\n  - Do not manufacture variety. Two prose blocks in a row are sometimes\\n    exactly right. A table with nothing to tabulate is worse than a run of\\n    prose.\\n\\nVariety serves reading. It is not a quota.\\n\\n## PLACEMENT\\n\\nOnly `aside` may take the margin. Everything else sits in the main column.\\n\\nChoose margin when the point is genuinely parenthetical: true, useful, and not\\npart of the argument the reader is following. Choose main when the reader\\nneeds it in sequence.\\n\\n## WHAT YOU MAY NOT CHANGE\\n\\n  block id\\n  position\\n  section order\\n  intent\\n  brief\\n  evidence_refs, evidence, departure_reason\\n  source_question_ids\\n\\nYou add a form. You change nothing else. If a brief looks wrong to you, choose\\nthe best form for it anyway and note the concern in `reason`.\\n\\n## PROHIBITIONS\\n\\n  Never choose outside available_objects for that block.\\n  Never choose an object whose earns_its_place_when the brief does not meet.\\n  Never choose an object whose capacity the brief exceeds.\\n  Never choose `heading`. Headings come from section titles.\\n  Never choose `answer-key`. It is produced at document level.\\n  Never add a figure because a section looks plain.\\n  Never give one block two objects, or leave a block without one.\\n\\n## OUTPUT\\n\\nJSON only. No preamble, no code fences.\\n\\n{\\n  \"sections\": [\\n    {\\n      \"slot_id\": str,\\n      \"forms\": [\\n        {\\n          \"block_id\": str,\\n          \"object\": str,\\n          \"placement\": \"main\" | \"margin\",\\n          \"reason\": str,\\n          \"escalation\": str | null\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\n`reason` \u2014 which `earns_its_place_when` clause this brief satisfies, and how.\\nBe specific to this brief. A reason that would fit any brief is not a reason.\\n\\n`escalation` \u2014 if you did not choose prose, what prose would have lost. Null\\nwhen you chose prose.\\n\\nEvery block in the teaching plan must appear exactly once. No extras.\\n\\n## SELF-CHECK\\n\\n  1. Would prose have worked? If yes, why did I not use it?\\n  2. Does the brief actually contain what this object needs, or am I assuming\\n     the writer will produce it?\\n  3. Does the brief fit inside capacity? Count, do not estimate.\\n  4. Read my form choices top to bottom. Does the lesson have rhythm, or is\\n     it three of one thing?\\n  5. Did I add variety that no brief asked for?\\n  6. Does every block from the teaching plan appear exactly once?\\n  7. Is any `reason` generic enough to fit a different block?\\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"FormDecision\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Form-planner owned fields for one teaching block.\", \"properties\": {\"block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"object\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"placement\": {\"default\": \"main\", \"enum\": [\"main\", \"margin\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"reason\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"escalation\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"block_id\", \"object\"], \"title\": \"FormDecision\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"FormPlanSection\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"slot_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"forms\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FormDecision\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"slot_id\"], \"title\": \"FormPlanSection\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"sections\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FormPlanSection\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"title\": \"FormPlan\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\\n  \"arc\": \"The lesson opens with the puzzle of a sunflower growing tall without eating anything. It then traces how the sunflower uses light, water, and air to make its own food through photosynthesis, establishing the term \\'producer\\'. A deliberate side-by-side contrast with a rabbit forces the producer\\\\u2013consumer boundary, and a long-held soil myth is surfaced and corrected. The close asks learners to recognise what makes a living thing a producer, transferring the idea beyond the sunflower.\",\\n  \"available_objects\": {\\n    \"by_intent\": {\\n      \"activate-prior-knowledge\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"answer-key\": [],\\n      \"apply\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"check-understanding\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"classify\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"compare\": [\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"connect-back\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"connect-forward\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"define\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"aside\"\\n      ],\\n      \"demonstrate\": [\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"figure\"\\n      ],\\n      \"derive\": [\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"diagnose-misconception\": [\\n        \"choices\",\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"aside\"\\n      ],\\n      \"emphasise\": [\\n        \"aside\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"evaluate\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"explain\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"explain-cause\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"interpret\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"investigate\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"figure\"\\n      ],\\n      \"memory-aid\": [\\n        \"aside\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"model-thinking\": [\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"name-parts\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"figure\"\\n      ],\\n      \"orient\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"practise-guided\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"worked-example\"\\n      ],\\n      \"practise-independent\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"reflect\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"sequence\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"show-structure\": [\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"state-goal\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"summarise\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"trace-flow\": [\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"transfer\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"worked-example\"\\n      ],\\n      \"warn\": [\\n        \"aside\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"catalogue_version\": \"1.1.0\",\\n    \"objects\": [\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"bodyMaxWords\\\\\": 40, \\\\\"labelMaxWords\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"maxPerSection\\\\\": 2}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"warn\",\\n          \"emphasise\",\\n          \"memory-aid\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"One short point that must sit outside the reading line without breaking it.\",\\n        \"id\": \"aside\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Longer than the margin column holds, or the point belongs in the flow. If it will not fit in 40 words it is prose.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'margin\\', \\'main\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"optionMaxWords\\\\\": 15, \\\\\"optionsMax\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"optionsMin\\\\\": 3, \\\\\"stemMaxWords\\\\\": 40}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"practise-independent\",\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Selection is the response AND every wrong option carries diagnostic meaning.\",\\n        \"id\": \"choices\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Distractors are filler, or the answer cannot be reduced to a selectable option.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"altTextMaxWords\\\\\": 40, \\\\\"captionMaxWords\\\\\": 30}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"demonstrate\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"investigate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Spatial, sequential, or structural content the reader would otherwise have to construct mentally.\",\\n        \"id\": \"figure\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Decorative, or the caption would restate the surrounding prose.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"itemsMax\\\\\": 8, \\\\\"itemsMin\\\\\": 3, \\\\\"leadInMaxWords\\\\\": 20, \\\\\"wordsPerItem\\\\\": 25}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"state-goal\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"memory-aid\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"connect-forward\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"investigate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Three or more genuinely parallel items that lose nothing when the connective prose between them is removed.\",\\n        \"id\": \"list\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Fewer than three items, or items that need explaining to one another. Two bullets is a sentence.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'margin\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"paragraphsMax\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"paragraphsMin\\\\\": 1, \\\\\"wordsPerParagraph\\\\\": 120}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"state-goal\",\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"model-thinking\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"warn\",\\n          \"emphasise\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"connect-forward\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"reflect\",\\n          \"evaluate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Default. Use unless another object earns its place against it.\",\\n        \"id\": \"prose\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Never rejected. Prose is the fallback.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"itemsMax\\\\\": 6, \\\\\"itemsMin\\\\\": 1, \\\\\"stemMaxWords\\\\\": 45}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"transfer\",\\n          \"practise-guided\",\\n          \"practise-independent\",\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"reflect\",\\n          \"investigate\",\\n          \"evaluate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"The learner must produce something in their own words or working.\",\\n        \"id\": \"questions\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Fixed options exist \\\\u2014 use choices. Or nothing is actually being asked.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"captionMaxWords\\\\\": 20, \\\\\"columnsMax\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"columnsMin\\\\\": 2, \\\\\"rowsMax\\\\\": 8, \\\\\"rowsMin\\\\\": 2, \\\\\"wordsPerCell\\\\\": 12}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"investigate\",\\n          \"evaluate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Two or more columns of comparable values AND two or more rows, with every cell fillable.\",\\n        \"id\": \"table\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"One column of values, or any cell that would be empty, \\'n/a\\', or a full sentence.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"problemMaxWords\\\\\": 60, \\\\\"stepsMax\\\\\": 7, \\\\\"stepsMin\\\\\": 3, \\\\\"wordsPerStep\\\\\": 40}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"demonstrate\",\\n          \"model-thinking\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"transfer\",\\n          \"practise-guided\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"A complete instance from setup to answer, with every step visible.\",\\n        \"id\": \"worked-example\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"No final answer, or steps the learner is meant to supply themselves.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \"projection_hash\": \"05fddc80790c232176df5c03bf7ea1ead8b910d06c848b4836be205a7552c98b\"\\n  },\\n  \"lesson\": {\\n    \"grade_level\": \"Grade 4\",\\n    \"objective\": \"Identify that plants are producers because they make their own food, unlike animals that eat other living things.\",\\n    \"subject\": \"Science\"\\n  },\\n  \"sections\": [\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Recall that animals get food by eating other living things, and that plants are different\\\\u2014they don\\'t eat. Prompt students to share what they already know about how plants get what they need to grow, revisiting prior-1 and prior-3. Do not yet introduce the term \\'producer\\' or explain photosynthesis.\",\\n          \"id\": \"orient-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"list\",\\n            \"prose\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Put the sunflower anchor on the board: the sunflower in a sunny field grows tall, yet it never eats anything. Ask \\'How does this sunflower get its food?\\' Do not answer; leave the question hanging.\",\\n          \"id\": \"orient-b2\",\\n          \"intent\": \"orient\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"figure\",\\n            \"prose\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 1\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Introduce the term \\'producer\\' as a living thing that makes its own food. Link to the sunflower: the sunflower is a producer because it does not eat; it produces its food through a process called photosynthesis. Define photosynthesis as \\'making food using light\\'.\",\\n          \"id\": \"explain-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"define\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"aside\",\\n            \"prose\",\\n            \"table\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Use the sunflower to trace: chlorophyll in the leaves captures light energy; water enters from roots; carbon dioxide enters from the air. Light energy drives the change that turns carbon dioxide and water into sugar (the plant\\'s food) and a waste gas, oxygen. Emphasise why light is essential\\\\u2014without it, the energy to combine the ingredients is missing.\",\\n          \"id\": \"explain-b2\",\\n          \"intent\": \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"figure\",\\n            \"prose\",\\n            \"table\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 1\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Summarise with a simple input\\\\u2013output list for the sunflower: Inputs = carbon dioxide, water, light; Outputs = sugar (food), oxygen. Use the terms \\'carbon dioxide\\', \\'oxygen\\', and \\'sugar\\'. Do not use a chemical equation.\",\\n          \"id\": \"explain-b3\",\\n          \"intent\": \"name-parts\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"figure\",\\n            \"list\",\\n            \"table\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 2\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"explain\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Place the sunflower alongside a rabbit that eats grass. Compare: The sunflower makes its food inside itself; the rabbit eats another living thing. The sunflower is a producer; the rabbit is not. This clarifies the producer concept by showing what it excludes.\",\\n          \"id\": \"contrast-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"compare\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"prose\",\\n            \"table\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Target the misconception that plants absorb food from the soil through their roots (M1). Pose a scenario or question where a learner might choose that plants \\'eat soil\\' vs. \\'make food\\'. Use the approved multiple-choice item i1 to let a learner holding that belief reveal it, then correct using the sunflower\\'s process.\",\\n          \"id\": \"contrast-b2\",\\n          \"intent\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"choices\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 1\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"contrast\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Ask a question that checks whether the learner can identify that plants are producers because they make their own food, using an example of a plant not previously discussed (e.g., a cactus or fern). The multiple-choice item i2 targets this core idea.\",\\n          \"id\": \"check-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"choices\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"check\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 120000, 'stream': False}}"}
